  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting, scale, mass and design, would be an overly bulky, discordant addition which would&nbsp;would appear overly dominant, would disrupt the rhythm of the street, and would result in the loss of open aspect to the corner plot. This would cause unacceptable harm to the character and appearance of the original dwelling and surrounding area. The differing roof forms would be conflicting and result in further discordance which would imbalance the terrace row.&nbsp;The proposal is therefore found to be at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals have regard to the existing character:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
